From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcrypt: the key derivation providers (PBKDF2, HKDF, SP800_56A_CONCAT, SP800_108_CTR_HMAC)

BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider(PBKDF2/HKDF/SP800_56A_CONCAT) was not supported (LibreOffice's xmlsec CNG back end asks
for them) and BCryptKeyDerivation did not exist. A key derivation provider's key (BCryptGenerateSymmetricKey) is
its secret; BCryptKeyDerivation runs PBKDF2 (RFC 8018: KDF_HASH_ALGORITHM, KDF_SALT, KDF_ITERATION_COUNT), HKDF
(RFC 5869: the HkdfHashAlgorithm, HkdfSaltAndFinalize and HkdfPrkAndFinalize key properties, KDF_HKDF_INFO), the
SP 800-56A concatenation KDF (KDF_ALGORITHMID, KDF_PARTYUINFO/VINFO, KDF_SUPPPUBINFO/PRIVINFO) and the SP 800-108
counter-mode KDF with HMAC (KDF_LABEL, KDF_CONTEXT), each written from its specification, with any of the hashes
including SHA-3; BCryptDeriveKey(secret, SP800_56A_CONCAT) runs the concatenation KDF over an agreed secret.
The providers have their pseudo-handles and enumerate as BCRYPT_KEY_DERIVATION_OPERATION.
---
